 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "Full Actors-pattern implementation (Governor + MarketEntry-LLM mock advisor + langgraph-clj StateGraph + append-only audit ledger + MemStore/DatomicStore via langchain-store.core), adapted from the cloud-itonami-iso3166-moz reference implementation (the closest architectural match: another catalog whose jurisdiction is NOT an OHADA member state) and cloud-itonami-iso3166-gin/-caf: src/marketentry/{facts,governor,phase,sim,operation,registry,store,marketentryllm}.cljc + full test suite (governor contract, store contract MemStore≡DatomicStore parity, registry pure-function, phase, facts) + src/statute/facts.cljc + docs/business-model.md + docs/operator-guide.md. The jurisdiction dossier (marketentry.facts) is grounded in ARMP's own government site (armp.mg/app.armp.mg) and the actual Loi n°2016-055 Code des Marchés Publics PDF read directly via pdftotext (Article 18 for ARMP's independent-authority status, Article 21 for exclusions/incapacities, Article 90 §IX-X for the flagship ineligibility-list mechanism), EDBM's own site (edbm.mg, the Economic Development Board of Madagascar) for business registration/RCS and general investment law (Loi n°2007-036), and the Direction Générale des Impôts' own site (impots.mg) for NIF/Code Général des Impôts. Both ARMP's and EDBM's live sites are now thin JS single-page apps with no server-rendered legal text, so this iteration used the Wayback Machine to read each site's own earlier, server-rendered content (disclosed explicitly in the facts.cljc namespace docstring). Madagascar's OHADA non-membership was independently re-verified directly against OHADA's own member-states page this session (not assumed by analogy to this fleet's -ben/-caf/-cog/-gin/-gnb siblings, all of which ARE OHADA members). The governor is SIX checks (not a richer sibling's seven -- no analog of a separate tax-ID-establishing-article check, mirroring cloud-itonami-iso3166-moz precedent), because the dossier does not ground a distinct NIF-establishing-article check separate from ordinary Article 21(c)/Article 90 ARMP exclusion screening. Facts this iteration could NOT independently confirm (EDBM's own founding decree/law number; the specific article establishing the NIF regime itself; an official Malagasy government-domain copy of the Code du Travail -- NATLEX returned a genuine Cloudflare bot-detection challenge this iteration did not attempt to bypass, so that one citation is sourced from a private aggregator via the Wayback Machine and flagged as such; an unresolved six-week date discrepancy between two independent sources' own citation of the Code du Travail's promulgation date) are stated as honest gaps in src/marketentry/facts.cljc's namespace docstring, not invented."}
